IMPORT prelude

-- Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015 (Singapore) -- what counts as liquor and as supplying it (s 2(1)), who is a repeat
-- offender (s 2(2)), the ban on unlicensed supply (s 4), the ban on drinking in a public place during a no-public drinking period
-- (s 12), drunkenness in public (s 14), the Liquor Control Zone uplift (s 16), banning notices and directions to leave a Liquor
-- Control Zone (ss 18 to 20), refusing a police request (ss 21, 22), false information (s 28) and the composition cap (s 33).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LCSCA2015.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 28 of 2017 ([28/2017], at s 2). The retrieval record calls it the current version as at
-- 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the law that decides where and when a person in Singapore may drink in
-- public, what happens to someone drunk in the street, and who may sell a beer. SCOPED to the provisions an individual meets. Not
-- encoded: licence grant, conditions, suspension and cancellation (ss 8, 9), trading hours of licensees (s 6) and premises (s 5),
-- signage (s 7), entry, closure and search powers (ss 10, 11, 23), the declaration of Liquor Control Zones (s 15), the cessation of
-- business order (s 17), consumption permits beyond their effect as an exception (s 13), appeals (ss 25 to 27), exemptions, arrest,
-- obstruction, corporate liability and regulations (ss 29 to 36). The no-public drinking period itself is PRESCRIBED by the Minister
-- (s 12(1), (2)) and is not in the Act, so it is an input here, not a clock.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Liquor Control (Supply and Consumption) Act 2015 -- drinking and supply`

GIVEN `first` IS A NUMBER, `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `first` AT MOST `second` THEN `first` ELSE `second`

§§ `2(1) -- liquor and supply`

-- "liquor" means (a) a beverage containing "more than 0.5% ethanol by mass or volume"; (b) a mixture of ethanol and another substance
-- containing more than 0.5% ethanol; or (c) any other substance prescribed by the regulations as liquor.
GIVEN `ethanol percent` IS A NUMBER, `prescribed as liquor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substance is liquor` IF
    `ethanol percent` GREATER THAN 0.5 OR `prescribed as liquor`

-- "supply" means (a) to "sell, barter or exchange the liquor (whether the reward or consideration is received ... specifically for the
-- liquor or as part of services or other goods sold ...)"; (b) to offer or agree to so sell, barter or exchange; or (c) to serve,
-- send, forward or deliver "in connection with such sale, barter or exchange". A gift with nothing given in return is not within the
-- words (an inference from the definition: no clause covers it).
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `selling a bottle`
    `bartering a bottle for goods`
    `offering a bottle for sale`
    `delivering a bottle that was sold`
    `serving drinks included in a paid package`
    `giving a bottle away for nothing`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is supply` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `giving a bottle away for nothing` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(2) -- repeat offender`

-- A person convicted of an offence under a provision is a repeat offender if "on at least one other occasion not earlier than 5 years
-- before" that conviction the person had been convicted under that same provision (or a listed predecessor provision).
GIVEN `has an earlier conviction under the same provision` IS A BOOLEAN, `years between the convictions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a repeat offender` IF
    `has an earlier conviction under the same provision` AND `years between the convictions` AT MOST 5

§§ `4 -- supply only under a liquor licence`

-- s 4(1): a person "must not supply any liquor unless the person is authorised by a liquor licence". (2) Not applicable to (a) delivery
-- only to a person, at that person's request, of liquor owned or ordered by that person; (b) an emergency where the liquor is necessary
-- to preserve life or prevent injury; (c) a religious service, ceremony or rite lawfully conducted by a priest or minister of religion
-- in a place of worship; (d) circumstances specified by Ministerial order in the Gazette.
DECLARE SupplyCircumstance IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary sale`
    `delivering liquor the recipient owns or ordered`
    `an emergency to preserve life or prevent injury`
    `a religious rite in a place of worship`
    `a circumstance specified by Ministerial order`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `licensed to supply` IS A BOOLEAN, `the supply circumstance` IS A SupplyCircumstance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply is an offence under section 4` IF
        `the dealing is supply` `the dealing`
    AND (NOT `licensed to supply`)
    AND CONSIDER `the supply circumstance`
        WHEN `an ordinary sale` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `12 -- drinking in a public place`

-- s 12(1): an individual "must not consume any liquor at any public place during any prescribed no-public drinking period applicable
-- to that place". (3) Not applicable to: (a) licensed premises where the licence allows consumption there AND it is during trading
-- hours; (b) consumption in accordance with a consumption permit in force for the place; (c) a prescribed public place in accordance
-- with prescribed conditions; (d) an emergency to preserve life or prevent injury; (e) a religious rite in a place of worship.
DECLARE DrinkingCircumstance IS ONE OF
    `drinking with no special circumstance`
    `at licensed premises allowing it, within trading hours`
    `at licensed premises after trading hours`
    `at licensed premises whose licence does not allow drinking there`
    `under a consumption permit for the place`
    `at a prescribed place within the prescribed conditions`
    `in an emergency to preserve life or prevent injury`
    `in a religious rite in a place of worship`

GIVEN `at a public place` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the no-public drinking period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the drinking circumstance` IS A DrinkingCircumstance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the drinking is an offence under section 12` IF
        `at a public place`
    AND `within the no-public drinking period`
    AND CONSIDER `the drinking circumstance`
        WHEN `at licensed premises allowing it, within trading hours` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `under a consumption permit for the place` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `at a prescribed place within the prescribed conditions` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `in an emergency to preserve life or prevent injury` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `in a religious rite in a place of worship` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `14 -- drunkenness in public`

-- s 14(6): an individual is drunk if (a) the individual's "speech, balance, coordination or behaviour is noticeably affected"; and
-- (b) it is reasonable to believe that this "is the result of the consumption of liquor".
GIVEN `noticeably affected` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably attributable to liquor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is drunk` IF
    `noticeably affected` AND `reasonably attributable to liquor`

-- s 14(1): drunk "and incapable of taking care of himself or herself in any public place". (2) while drunk, appears in a public place
-- or in premises "which it is a trespass for the individual to enter", and there conducts himself or herself so as to "cause annoyance
-- to any person".
GIVEN `noticeably affected` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably attributable to liquor` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `incapable of taking care of oneself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `drunk and incapable is an offence under section 14(1)` IF
    `the individual is drunk` `noticeably affected` `reasonably attributable to liquor` AND `in a public place` AND `incapable of taking care of oneself`

GIVEN `noticeably affected` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably attributable to liquor` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `trespassing on premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `causing annoyance to someone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `drunken annoyance is an offence under section 14(2)` IF
        `the individual is drunk` `noticeably affected` `reasonably attributable to liquor`
    AND (`in a public place` OR `trespassing on premises`)
    AND `causing annoyance to someone`

§§ `4, 12, 14, 16, 19 to 22, 28 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 4(3): $20,000; repeat offender $20,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 12(4): $1,000; repeat offender $2,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 14(1): $1,000 or one month or both; repeat offender $2,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 14(2) and s 14(4) (failing to leave when directed under s 14(3)(a)): $1,000 or 6 months or both; repeat offender $2,000 or
-- 6 MONTHS or both -- a repeat offender faces the same prison term as a first offender.
-- s 19(1) (breaching a banning notice), s 20(4) (breaching a direction to leave or not enter a zone), s 21(2) (failing to state name,
-- residence, or how the liquor was acquired), s 22(2) (failing to allow inspection): $2,500 or 3 months or both. No repeat uplift.
-- s 28 (knowingly or recklessly giving false or misleading information): $5,000; repeat offender $10,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 16: an offence under section 4, 12 or 14 "committed within a Liquor Control Zone" is liable to "not more than one and a half times
-- the respective penalties". Applied here to both fine and imprisonment, since s 16 says "penalties" without distinction.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed supply`
    `drinking in public in the no-public drinking period`
    `being drunk and incapable in public`
    `drunken annoyance`
    `ignoring a direction to leave`
    `breaching a banning notice`
    `breaching a direction to leave a zone`
    `refusing to give name or residence`
    `refusing an inspection`
    `giving false information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the zone uplift applies to` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed supply` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `drinking in public in the no-public drinking period` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `being drunk and incapable in public` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `drunken annoyance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ignoring a direction to leave` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed supply` THEN 20000
    WHEN `drinking in public in the no-public drinking period` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `being drunk and incapable in public` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `drunken annoyance` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `ignoring a direction to leave` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000
    OTHERWISE 2500

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed supply` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 3 ELSE 0
    WHEN `drinking in public in the no-public drinking period` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 3 ELSE 0
    WHEN `being drunk and incapable in public` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 3 ELSE 1
    WHEN `drunken annoyance` THEN 6
    WHEN `ignoring a direction to leave` THEN 6
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 3 ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 3

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `in a Liquor Control Zone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the zone multiplier` MEANS
    IF `in a Liquor Control Zone` AND `the zone uplift applies to` `the offence` THEN 1.5 ELSE 1

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a Liquor Control Zone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    `the base maximum fine` `the offence` `repeat` TIMES `the zone multiplier` `the offence` `in a Liquor Control Zone`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN, `in a Liquor Control Zone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    `the base maximum months of imprisonment` `the offence` `repeat` TIMES `the zone multiplier` `the offence` `in a Liquor Control Zone`

§§ `18, 19 -- Liquor Control Zone banning notices`

-- s 18(1): may be given if the Commissioner or an authorised officer "suspects, on reasonable grounds, the individual of committing or
-- having committed an offence under section 12 or 14 wholly or partly in a Liquor Control Zone". (3) no right to be heard first.
-- (4) the period "must not exceed 30 days".
GIVEN `suspected of a section 12 or 14 offence in a zone` IS A BOOLEAN, `days banned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the banning notice is within power` IF
    `suspected of a section 12 or 14 offence in a zone` AND `days banned` AT MOST 30

-- s 19(1): an offence if the individual "without reasonable excuse" enters, remains, or attempts to, in contravention of the notice.
-- (2) the notice does not prevent entering or remaining "for the purpose of the individual residing" there "or attending to the
-- individual's usual place of residence or work" there, or entering in accordance with the exceptions specified in the notice.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `going for a drink`
    `going home`
    `going to work`
    `visiting a friend`
    `within an exception stated in the notice`

GIVEN `entered or remained in the banned area` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry breaches the banning notice` IF
        `entered or remained in the banned area`
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND CONSIDER `the purpose`
        WHEN `going home` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `going to work` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `within an exception stated in the notice` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `20 -- directions to leave or not enter a zone`

-- s 20(2): unless the entrant is arrested, a police officer or approved person may direct an entrant to leave and not re-enter, or
-- refuse entry, "for a stated reasonable time of not more than 24 hours".
GIVEN `arrested` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours stated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the zone direction is within power` IF
    (NOT `arrested`) AND `hours stated` AT MOST 24

§§ `33 -- composition`

-- s 33(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for a sum "not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) $5,000.
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can be collected to compound` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
